              Verdant Hearth uses a transparent two-tier data architecture:
            </p>
            <ul class="space-y-2 text-xs text-[var(--text-muted)] mb-6">
              <li>1. <strong>Without API (Demo Mode):</strong> If <code>PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL</code> is omitted, all queries and form submissions fall back gracefully to local typed mock data in <code>src/data/restaurant.ts</code>.</li>
              <li>2. <strong>With API Connected:</strong> Once <code>PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL</code> is defined, <code>src/lib/data.ts</code> and <code>src/lib/api.ts</code> route requests to your live REST backend.</li>
              <li>3. <strong>Static Build vs. Live Submissions:</strong> Content like menu dishes, artisan profiles, and stories are rendered at static build time. When menu data changes in your backend database, trigger a webhook rebuild on your host (e.g., Vercel Deploy Hook). Interactive forms (Reservations, Contact, Newsletter) submit live <code>POST</code> requests via client fetch directly to your API.</li>
            </ul>

